# motion-reset (plan section 6, M10): FV 05's Reset all filmstrip. The values typed on both sides
# (2(x + 1)/1.5)² + 1: a 2, k 1, b 1.5, h −1; the field of each box in the reference's DOM at
# 1440 x 900: a's (352.5, 413.5, 62 x 22), k's 457.5, b's 518.5, h's 562.5), each a jump, then a
# press on the top bar's empty middle (760, 48) takes the focus off and the jumps settle. Reset all
# (358.12, 366.5, 84.88 x 20 in the Transform head: its centre (400, 376)) clicked: a, b, h and k
# spring back together on the sweep spring (1 / 170 / 26: 28, 62, 82, 92, 99 % at 80 … 480 ms,
# at rest at 702), P riding the curve at x = 2, the Original under it until the curve lands on it;
# each changed term flashes (in 80 ms, held, gone by 600). The frames at 0, 80 … 480 ms, then at
# rest. Chromium focuses Reset all on the click and hands the focus to a's box (a's unit box lit),
# as the port does; WebKit's click focuses no button (plan call 3 f).
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
click 383 424
wait 16
type "2"
key Enter
click 383 468
wait 16
type "1"
key Enter
click 383 529
wait 16
type "1.5"
key Enter
click 383 573
wait 16
type "-1"
key Enter
click 760 48
wait 1000
shot set
click 400 376
frames reset every 80 for 480
wait 520
shot reset-rest
